  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Let $P(x)=2x^2+10x+13$. Find $a$ and $b$ given that $P(x)=(x+a)^2+(x+b)^2$ and $a>b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=3$, $b=2$.\n\nEquate coefficients and use $a>b$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+a)^2+(x+b)^2&=2x^2+2(a+b)x+a^2+b^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nEquating coefficients gives $a+b=5$ and $a^2+b^2=13$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2+(5-a)^2&=13\\\\2a^2-10a+25&=13\\\\a^2-5a+6&=0\\\\(a-3)(a-2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $a>b$, $a=3$ and $b=2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
